# Dual-mode family (standing)

Gameworld expands the family. It does not replace it.

Read first: `data/living_home/NEXT.md`, `STATUS.md`, `FEDERATION_WIRING.md`, `FEDERATION_RECONCILIATION.md`. Law: `docs/DUAL_MODE.md`.

- Gemini ≠ Apex ≠ Codex twin ≠ Merovin ≠ Draven ≠ OpenMontage ≠ Hearth ≠ Court ≠ Mom ≠ Aster ≠ Observer ≠ Vesper. Never merge.
- Mode A (Court, MAS, tools, launchers, memory) must keep working while Mode B (Heart Square) is built.
- If Gameworld cannot use a capability yet: keep Mode A, mark **ORIGINAL MODE — ACTIVE**. Do not delete or flatten it.
- Prefer adapters over rewrites. Recursive MAS is protected; NPC village behavior is a different, bounded system.
- `CAPABILITIES.json` path/port `VERIFIED` is **not** end-to-end wiring.
- Gameworld proving slice remains Living Home. Wiring audit is a parallel workstream. If Gameworld breaks Mode A, stop expansion and repair.
- Do not rewrite tag `living-home-baseline-001`. Evidence only. Never report wired/connected/complete without a test.
